obj2 = {'name': 'John', 'email': 'john@example.com'}

# Circular reference:
obj3 = {'name': 'John', 'email': 'john@example.com', 'self': obj3}

# Compare two valid objects:
compare_json(obj1, obj2)  # True

# Compare two objects with a circular reference:
compare_json(obj3, obj3)  # True
```

**Time Complexity:**

The time complexity of the `compare_json()` function is O(n), where n is the size of the JSON objects. This is because the `rec_compare()` function performs a depth-first traversal of the JSON objects, visiting each node only once.

