response:
```java
class ProgrammingLanguage {

    private String name;

    public ProgrammingLanguage(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }
}

class ProgrammingLanguageManager {

    private List<ProgrammingLanguage> languages = new ArrayList<>();

    public void addLanguage(String language) {
        languages.add(new ProgrammingLanguage(language));
    }

    public void removeLanguage(String language) {
        languages.remove(new ProgrammingLanguage(language));
    }

    public String[] getLanguages() {
        return languages.stream().map(ProgrammingLanguage::getName).sorted().toArray(String[]::new);
    }

    public boolean isLanguagePresent(String language) {
        return languages.stream().anyMatch(p -> p.getName().equals(language));
    }
}
```

**Explanation:**

* The `ProgrammingLanguage` class represents a single programming language.
* The `ProgrammingLanguageManager` class has a list of `ProgrammingLanguage` objects.
* The `addLanguage()` method adds a new language to the list.
* The `removeLanguage()` method removes a language from the list.
* The `getLanguages()` method returns an array of all languages in alphabetical order.
* The `isLanguagePresent()` method checks if a specific language is already in the list.

**Usage:**

```java
ProgrammingLanguageManager manager = new ProgrammingLanguageManager();
manager.addLanguage("JAVA");
manager.addLanguage("PYTHON");
manager.addLanguage("GO");
manager.addLanguage("RUST");

// Check if language is present
System.out.println(manager.isLanguagePresent("PYTHON")); // Output: true

// Get list of languages
System.out.println(manager.getLanguages()); // Output: [GO, JAVA, PYTHON, RUST]

// Remove language
manager.removeLanguage("JAVA");

// Get list of languages again
System.out.println(manager.getLanguages()); // Output: [GO, PYTHON, RUST]
```

