**Code for CKY Parsing:**

```c
void cky_parse(char *sentence, int len) {
    int i, j, k;
    char **words = malloc(sizeof(char *) * len);
    for (i = 0; i < len; i++) {
        words[i] = malloc(sizeof(char) * 20);
    }

    // Split sentence into words
    for (i = 0, j = 0; i < len; i++) {
        if (sentence[i] == ' ') {
            words[j][0] = '\0';
            j++;
        } else {
            words[j][i - j] = sentence[i];
        }
    }

    // Initialize CKY table
    int **cky = malloc(sizeof(int *) * len);
    for (i = 0; i < len; i++) {
        cky[i] = malloc(sizeof(int) * len);
    }

    // Fill CKY table
    for (i = 0; i < len; i++) {
        for (j = i; j < len; j++) {
            cky[i][j] = -1;
        }
    }

    for (k = 2; k < len; k++) {
        for (i = 0; i < len - k + 1; i++) {
            j = i + k - 1;
            if (words[i][0] == words[j][0] && cky[i][j - 1] != -1) {
                cky[i][j] = cky[i][j - 1];
            }
        }
    }

    // Find the length of the longest common substring
    int max_len = 0;
    for (i = 0; i < len; i++) {
        max_len = MAX(max_len, cky[i][len - 1]);
    }

    // Print the result
    printf("The longest common substring is of length %d.\n", max_len);
}
```

**Explanation:**

* **Split Sentence:** The function first splits the given sentence into words.


* **CKY Table Initialization:** It initializes a CKY table, which is a 2D matrix that will store the length of the longest common substring for each pair of words.


* **CKY Table Filling:** It fills the CKY table by iterating over the words and finding the longest common substring length for each pair of words.


* **Longest Common Substring Length:** It finds the length of the longest common substring by checking the values in the CKY table.


* **Output:** It prints the length of the longest common substring.

