```java
public boolean isMazeValid(int[][] matrix) {
    int rows = matrix.length;
    int cols = matrix[0].length;

    // Check if the start and end points are blocked
    if (matrix[0][0] == 1 || matrix[rows - 1][cols - 1] == 1) {
        return false;
    }

    // Initialize a visited array to keep track of visited cells
    boolean[][] visited = new boolean[rows][cols];

    // Start DFS from the top-left corner
    dfs(matrix, 0, 0, rows, cols, visited);

    // Check if all cells are visited
    for (int i = 0; i < rows; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < cols; j++) {
            if (!visited[i][j]) {
                return false;
            }
        }
    }

    return true;
}

private void dfs(int[][] matrix, int row, int col, int rows, int cols, boolean[][] visited) {
    visited[row][col] = true;

    // Check if the cell is the end point
    if (row == rows - 1 && col == cols - 1) {
        return;
    }

    // Check neighbors
    if (row > 0 && matrix[row - 1][col] == 0 && !visited[row - 1][col]) {
        dfs(matrix, row - 1, col, rows, cols, visited);
    }
    if (col > 0 && matrix[row][col - 1] == 0 && !visited[row][col - 1]) {
        dfs(matrix, row, col - 1, rows, cols, visited);
    }
    if (row < rows - 1 && matrix[row + 1][col] == 0 && !visited[row + 1][col]) {
        dfs(matrix, row + 1, col, rows, cols, visited);
    }
    if (col < cols - 1 && matrix[row][col + 1] == 0 && !visited[row][col + 1]) {
        dfs(matrix, row, col + 1, rows, cols, visited);
    }
}
```

**Explanation:**

* The `isMazeValid` function checks if the maze is valid by performing a Depth-First Search (DFS) algorithm on the matrix.
* It starts by initializing a visited array to keep track of the cells that have been visited during the DFS.
* The DFS function recursively explores the maze, marking cells as visited and stopping when the end point is reached.
* The `isMazeValid` function then checks if all cells in the maze have been visited, indicating the presence of a clear path from the top-left corner to the bottom-right corner.
* The `dfs` function recursively explores the maze, visiting neighboring cells if they are open and not yet visited.

