```javascript
function extractAttributes(htmlTag: string): { url: string, class: string } {
  const regex = /<a\s+([^>]+)>/gm;
  const match = htmlTag.match(regex);

  if (!match) {
    throw new Error('Invalid HTML tag.');
  }

  const attributes = match[1].split(/\s+/);

  const url = attributes.find(attribute => attribute.startsWith('href="'))?.replace('href="', '').trim() || '';
  const className = attributes.find(attribute => attribute.startsWith('class="'))?.replace('class="', '').trim() || '';

  return { url, class: className };
}
```

**Explanation:**

* The function uses a regular expression to extract the attributes of the anchor tag.
* `match[1]` returns the attributes string after the opening `<a>` tag.
* `attributes.find()` iterates over the attributes and returns the attribute value based on the attribute name.
* `replace()` function removes the attribute prefix and trims the value.
* If no URL or class attribute is found, the function returns an empty string or `null` respectively.

**Example Usage:**

```javascript
const htmlTag = `<a href="<?php echo base_url('gioi-thieu-dich-vu.html')?>"
   class="btn btn-primary animated bounceIn delay-1s" style="margin: 20px 0px; padding: 12px" >TÌM HIỂU THÊM</a>`;

const result = extractAttributes(htmlTag);

console.log(result);
```

