```java
import java.io.*;
import java.util.*;

public class PatternFinder {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String sourceFilePath = UIUtils.getSelectedFile();

        try {
            // Read the file contents
            BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(sourceFilePath));
            String line;
            StringBuilder content = new StringBuilder();
            while ((line = br.readLine()) != null) {
                content.append(line + "\n");
            }
            br.close();

            // Search for the pattern
            String pattern = "your_pattern";
            List<Integer> positions = new ArrayList<>();
            int index = content.indexOf(pattern);
            while (index >= 0) {
                positions.add(index);
                index = content.indexOf(pattern, index + 1);
            }

            // Display the results
            System.out.println("Occurrences of '" + pattern + "':");
            for (int position : positions) {
                int lineNumber = 1;
                int charOffset = position;
                for (int i = 0; i < position; i++) {
                    if (content.charAt(i) == '\n') {
                        lineNumber++;
                    }
                }
                System.out.println("Line: " + lineNumber + ", Character Offset: " + charOffset);
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```

**Explanation:**

* The `UIUtils.getSelectedFile` method retrieves the path of the selected file.
* The `BufferedReader` class is used to read the file contents line by line.
* The `StringBuilder` class is used to accumulate the file contents.
* The `indexOf` method searches for the specified pattern and returns the index of its first occurrence.
* The positions of each occurrence are stored in an `ArrayList`.
* The program iterates over the `positions` list and prints the line number and character offset of each occurrence.

**Note:**

* Replace `"your_pattern"` with the actual pattern you want to search for.
* The code snippet provided does not include error handling for invalid file paths or patterns.

