```java
public class PrimeDigitSum {

    public static int sumPrimeDigits(int n) {
        if (n == 0) {
            return 0;
        }

        int sum = 0;

        while (n > 0) {
            int remainder = n % 10;
            if (isPrime(remainder)) {
                sum += remainder;
            }
            n /= 10;
        }

        return sum;
    }

    private static boolean isPrime(int number) {
        if (number < 2) {
            return false;
        }

        return number == 2 || number % 2 != 0 && number % 3 != 0 && isPrimeHelper(number, 5, 2);
    }

    private static boolean isPrimeHelper(int number, int i, int j) {
        if (number % i == 0) {
            return false;
        }

        if (i * i > number) {
            return true;
        }

        return isPrimeHelper(number, i + j, j);
    }
}
```

**Explanation:**

* **sumPrimeDigits()** function iterates over the digits of the input integer n by dividing it by 10 until it reaches 0.
* **isPrime()** function checks if a given number is prime or not. It employs a optimized helper function isPrimeHelper() for efficient primality determination.
* **isPrimeHelper()** function iteratively checks if a number is divisible by any prime number from 5 onwards. If it finds any factor, it returns false; otherwise, it returns true when it reaches the square root of the number.

**Complexity:**

* Space Complexity: O(1)
* Time Complexity: O(log n), where n is the absolute value of the input integer.

